<h2>Florida Car Insurance – What’s Not Covered:</h2>
<ol>
<li><strong>Regular Maintenance and Wear and Tear:</strong> Routine maintenance like oil changes, tire rotations, and general wear and tear are not covered under car insurance policies.</li>
<li><strong>Mechanical Failures:</strong> Issues like engine breakdowns or transmission problems fall outside the scope of car insurance and are typically covered by warranties or service contracts.</li>
<li><strong>Certain Exclusions:</strong> Specific situations, such as intentional damage or using your personal car for commercial purposes like ridesharing, might not be covered. Always check your policy for detailed exclusions.</li>
</ol>
